  "goodToKnow": "Radeln is a colloquial, especially southern German word for cycling: Rad fahren. It takes sein: Wir sind geradelt. Each year thousands of municipalities take part in Stadtradeln, a campaign where people log kilometres cycled for the climate. Der Radler is a cyclist and also, in Bavaria, a shandy (beer with lemonade). Don't confuse it with rodeln (to sledge)."
